WEBVTT

00:06.940 --> 00:08.980
Aoshi piggybacked me all the way home.

00:10.440 --> 00:14.990
When I was looking up from his back, the color of the sky I saw that day

00:14.990 --> 00:17.370
is something that strangely
remains in my heart to this day.

00:18.870 --> 00:23.040
It was ridiculously blue and
tremendously discomforting.

00:24.580 --> 00:28.250
And to think you're going to
take me somewhere again...

00:32.010 --> 00:33.170
Aoshi.

00:42.100 --> 00:47.690
The Dark Metal

00:42.140 --> 00:42.180
The Dark Metal

00:47.690 --> 00:52.110
Night turns to day, and day turns to night. Our wishes have wilted away

00:52.110 --> 00:56.280
Where did the person I want to meet go?

00:56.280 --> 01:00.740
Interlocking these fingers with my beloved

01:00.740 --> 01:04.500
Even though I can't feel them, I continue to live

01:04.540 --> 01:09.130
When the flower's petals

01:09.130 --> 01:13.260
Are plucked off by the wind's playful gale

01:13.260 --> 01:17.720
They are scattered in every direction

01:17.720 --> 01:23.060
Even if you long for it

01:24.060 --> 01:28.770
Don't disappear, just don't

01:28.770 --> 01:32.570
I can even give everything else away if I have to

01:32.570 --> 01:37.410
You were there, and I was there with you

01:37.410 --> 01:41.740
Let me take in these memories

01:41.740 --> 01:48.670
These brief moments are connected, turning it into eternity

02:06.980 --> 02:11.980
Episode 10
Your Song

02:15.690 --> 02:17.950
The Argent has entered the Lightless Realm.

02:17.950 --> 02:20.410
No anomalies so far.

02:20.410 --> 02:22.160
Roger that. Return and stand by.

02:22.160 --> 02:23.280
Roger.

02:28.960 --> 02:29.790
Iwato?

02:31.630 --> 02:35.130
Why the hell did he come back?

02:36.210 --> 02:40.130
For him to come back after deciding to quit...

02:40.130 --> 02:41.470
It's not like him.

02:41.930 --> 02:46.310
Maybe he realized that he was the only one who can do it?

02:47.140 --> 02:48.680
I wonder if that's really the case.

02:59.070 --> 03:01.240
We have nothing to worry about, right?

03:02.950 --> 03:06.580
He's gonna come back safe and sound, right?

03:06.580 --> 03:07.580
I don't know.

03:09.080 --> 03:15.090
Perhaps it is salvation for Akashi to die in there.

03:16.300 --> 03:18.800
He looked in pain all this time.

03:18.800 --> 03:23.890
Like he was getting crushed under the pressure from everything happening around him.

03:24.390 --> 03:29.600
And dying within the machine that his older
brother used to pilot may finally release him.

03:30.060 --> 03:33.350
How can you say that?

03:34.360 --> 03:35.650
You're right.

03:35.650 --> 03:37.480
I'm sorry, Sasame.

03:37.480 --> 03:41.820
I was just thinking maybe that's what happiness is for Akashi.

03:42.410 --> 03:45.910
Happiness for Akashi-kun?

03:49.250 --> 03:51.960
Suzaki here... Connection...

03:51.960 --> 03:55.330
Unknown... Be very careful... Keep confirming... time...

03:56.170 --> 03:57.340
The comm's gone out already?

04:07.760 --> 04:11.020
Was that your memory just now?

04:11.020 --> 04:13.390
Don't butt in without permission.

04:13.980 --> 04:17.150
I promised I'd get back home.

04:17.900 --> 04:18.770
Kasane...

04:19.570 --> 04:21.440
Akashi...

04:21.440 --> 04:26.070
Yeah, you were a good brother
to the very end. You truly were.

04:27.120 --> 04:31.410
So don't come out at each and every opportunity!

04:37.130 --> 04:40.550
I told him to avoid as much combat as possible,

04:40.550 --> 04:44.760
but I'm worried that he might create another Admonition.

04:45.090 --> 04:48.010
If that does happen, I hope he retreats immediately.

04:48.350 --> 04:53.230
I don't think Akashi has enough negative
emotions to create an Admonition anymore.

04:53.730 --> 04:54.730
Besides...

04:54.730 --> 04:57.650
Oh, never mind...

04:57.650 --> 05:01.110
If you can't say it, don't leak out bits and pieces.

05:01.110 --> 05:02.150
Sorry.

05:02.150 --> 05:07.410
In any case, you have other grounds
to assert that Akashi will return safely.

05:07.820 --> 05:12.040
Either way, we can't support him if he's inside the Lightless Realm.

05:12.500 --> 05:15.920
Unlike Admonitions that are created from cores,

05:15.920 --> 05:20.380
one has to calm down the mental
state of the person used to create it.

05:20.840 --> 05:23.090
So everything rests on Akashi.

05:23.420 --> 05:28.470
The moment that he dies would be when the Admonition disappears.

05:29.140 --> 05:31.810
Uh, well...

05:34.980 --> 05:37.060
Sorry about that...

05:45.570 --> 05:47.990
Where are you, Heito?

05:47.990 --> 05:49.660
If you're around, hurry up and show yourself!

05:59.920 --> 06:01.290
You again?

06:32.620 --> 06:33.620
Figures...

07:00.940 --> 07:05.360
So you won't be gone until I disappear too.

07:16.540 --> 07:19.910
Maybe it's better for me to just die.

07:19.910 --> 07:23.130
You're the one who deserves to die most.

07:24.920 --> 07:28.460
Someone who seriously thinks that should just...

07:37.640 --> 07:41.640
Why did I come here again?

07:41.640 --> 07:44.270
I won't end up the same way Aoshi did.

07:44.270 --> 07:46.690
I'm not him.

07:48.070 --> 07:50.490
I'm not my brother?

07:50.490 --> 07:53.780
Why do you have to be the one to go?

07:53.780 --> 07:55.910
Someone has to do it.

07:56.160 --> 07:57.160
But...

07:57.830 --> 07:59.660
I'll make sure I come back.

08:01.000 --> 08:04.920
I actually don't want to go.

08:05.420 --> 08:07.710
I don't want to go, Kasane-san!

08:08.210 --> 08:11.590
Is this my memory?

08:11.590 --> 08:15.050
No, it's getting all tangled up with Aoshi's memories.

08:15.680 --> 08:16.680
Dammit.

08:25.480 --> 08:27.270
What the hell is that?!

08:37.950 --> 08:41.370
I have to get back home.

08:49.210 --> 08:51.050
Come back...

08:55.630 --> 08:56.430
Wha—

08:59.310 --> 09:00.060
Akashi-kun.

09:04.810 --> 09:06.100
Come back.

09:07.520 --> 09:08.980
Akashi...

09:09.360 --> 09:10.440
Sasame?

09:10.860 --> 09:13.070
Come back, Akashi...

09:13.490 --> 09:14.900
No...

09:45.560 --> 09:49.610
I feel like I'm not gonna be able to differentiate between Aoshi's memories and mine.

09:52.480 --> 09:54.530
I shouldn't inhale that light.

10:06.330 --> 10:08.500
In regards to time, we still have some to spare.

10:13.130 --> 10:18.090
The place with no light swallows
everything and conceives everything.

10:18.760 --> 10:22.510
Emotions take a turn for the worse,
and your reasoning and psyche are crushed.

10:34.230 --> 10:36.570
Where is this?

10:44.080 --> 10:47.500
Getting off the Reaper is sickening in its own way.

10:47.500 --> 10:49.370
My mind feels like it's going to melt.

10:55.840 --> 10:57.050
Oh, right.

10:57.050 --> 10:59.300
How long have I been in here for?

10:59.300 --> 11:01.010
I have to check...

11:03.390 --> 11:04.350
Heito?

11:19.030 --> 11:19.950
Emiru...

11:21.240 --> 11:22.570
Are you...

11:23.490 --> 11:25.330
Are you really there?

11:35.170 --> 11:36.460
Are you crying?

11:37.170 --> 11:39.260
Do you have a grudge? Are you cursing me?

11:40.470 --> 11:43.180
It's really tough, isn't it, Emiru?

11:44.300 --> 11:45.390
Akashi.

11:46.970 --> 11:49.520
Akashi, I was waiting for you.

11:51.020 --> 11:52.440
I wanted to see you.

12:01.360 --> 12:05.870
I wanted to see you all this time.

12:06.410 --> 12:09.580
So it really was true after all, Emiru.

12:10.370 --> 12:12.000
You really are...

12:13.250 --> 12:17.000
I'm glad I was able to see you one last time.

12:23.760 --> 12:24.680
The Corpse?

12:36.110 --> 12:38.690
One more has been swallowed.

12:38.690 --> 12:44.450
You search and search, but all you find are pieces of emotions you don't want to know about.

12:46.030 --> 12:46.990
Emiru!

13:08.300 --> 13:09.180
It's no good.

13:20.690 --> 13:23.690
I'm completely lost.

13:31.040 --> 13:32.410
I feel so heavy...

13:34.710 --> 13:38.710
This suit's starting to turn into Necrometal too.

13:39.170 --> 13:42.760
I'll probably start to soon...

13:43.380 --> 13:45.340
I'm so tired.

13:45.340 --> 13:46.930
I don't care anymore...

13:46.930 --> 13:48.140
Just like this...

13:49.010 --> 13:50.140
We're going home.

13:55.020 --> 13:58.810
Aoshi, were you lost too?

13:58.810 --> 14:01.690
You were lost and came out?

14:01.690 --> 14:04.860
Nothing makes sense in here, seriously.

14:05.530 --> 14:06.780
I'm going home.

14:08.490 --> 14:10.200
I have to go home.

14:16.040 --> 14:18.250
Because Kasane-san is waiting.

14:20.330 --> 14:23.170
You always had someone waiting for you.

14:26.630 --> 14:29.510
I'll make sure to get home.

14:33.430 --> 14:39.390
After you died—no, wait,
you're still not really dead yet.

14:40.850 --> 14:42.940
Either way, I don't care.

14:43.940 --> 14:46.740
After they told me you were dead,

14:46.690 --> 14:50.570
it felt as if a heavy burden had been lifted from my shoulders.

14:50.910 --> 14:55.330
I probably smiled...

14:56.410 --> 15:00.420
I'm probably spouting stuff I don't need to, but...

15:00.420 --> 15:04.710
I feel like my mind is going to melt if I don't talk.

15:04.710 --> 15:07.840
I'm glad that you're with me.

15:09.090 --> 15:13.180
This is the first time I ever thought that way.

15:13.600 --> 15:17.560
You were the weight pinning me down all this time.

15:18.430 --> 15:20.890
I was always being compared to you.

15:21.980 --> 15:23.230
Do you remember?

15:23.900 --> 15:28.900
Back when I was a kid, I got hurt, and you piggybacked me home.

15:29.900 --> 15:32.870
And I thought to myself, "Why's he
doing something he doesn't need to?"

15:33.870 --> 15:35.490
It's always the same.

15:36.240 --> 15:38.620
You get praised.

15:38.620 --> 15:40.870
All because you brought your
useless little brother home.

15:42.120 --> 15:46.630
But I was depressed and didn't want to go home.

15:48.090 --> 15:51.800
I even hated the fact that the
sky was optimistically blue.

15:52.680 --> 15:59.680
And after we got home, I wasn't scolded or fretted over. I was just abandoned.

16:01.230 --> 16:08.730
That's how things were imprinted in my head—
that nobody would ever wait for me to come back.

16:09.780 --> 16:15.450
That's why when someone out
there needed me, I didn't notice—

16:15.450 --> 16:18.950
or rather, I went out of my way not to notice.

16:20.250 --> 16:24.000
I wish you were the one I synchronized with.

16:37.260 --> 16:39.640
If I could see Emiru right now,

16:40.970 --> 16:41.890
I'd be more...

16:47.060 --> 16:48.320
Let's go home.

16:48.320 --> 16:49.480
Just a little more.

16:49.480 --> 16:52.030
What do you mean by just a bit more?

16:52.780 --> 16:58.530
Kasane-san isn't in a place like this...

16:59.030 --> 17:00.040
Akashi-kun!

17:14.220 --> 17:23.350
Toss a coconut onto the black of Corpses...

17:23.350 --> 17:28.230
Suspicions of Charon and Garon...

17:28.230 --> 17:36.530
One, meddling in affairs of crying children...

17:30.270 --> 17:31.980
This song...

17:37.280 --> 17:43.950
Two, burn the bones of crying children...

17:42.540 --> 17:43.950
Please come back...

17:43.950 --> 17:52.300
Three, atop the carcass is a crying child...

17:45.040 --> 17:46.040
Sasame...

17:47.370 --> 17:50.460
Can you sing it one more time?

17:51.000 --> 17:51.920
I want to hear it.

17:52.920 --> 17:56.510
Quiet, just be quiet, suspicions of the Corpses...

17:56.510 --> 18:01.680
Scattered into ashes, here, Garon...

17:58.760 --> 18:00.260
I'm waiting for you.

18:02.890 --> 18:03.970
Sasame!

18:26.910 --> 18:28.330
The Reaper...

18:28.710 --> 18:30.130
So that's how it is.

18:30.130 --> 18:32.000
Just a bit more...

18:32.000 --> 18:35.960
Are you saying you brought me all the way here?

18:36.760 --> 18:37.920
Aoshi...

18:47.560 --> 18:49.270
You helped Akashi?

18:51.270 --> 18:54.020
You sang for Akashi, didn't you?

18:55.980 --> 19:00.490
Harsher things may be waiting for him if he comes back.

19:00.820 --> 19:03.580
Are you saying I should've just abandoned him?

19:03.580 --> 19:04.910
That's not it.

19:05.580 --> 19:09.460
But what is it you want Akashi to do once he comes back, Sasame?

19:29.430 --> 19:33.770
This is Aoshi's memory...

19:39.780 --> 19:41.660
How comforting.

19:41.660 --> 19:46.490
This is the first time I've felt comfort within the Reaper.

19:52.460 --> 19:53.880
You're still showing up?

20:13.400 --> 20:18.900
That's right! I was always protected by you!

20:18.900 --> 20:21.990
You were always waiting for me!

20:25.030 --> 20:30.120
I didn't understand such a simple thing!

20:52.640 --> 20:56.520
I beg of you. Take me back home again.

20:58.320 --> 21:00.110
Carry me on your back like before.

21:06.200 --> 21:08.410
Let's go home, Big Brother.

21:11.410 --> 21:13.870
We've got a signal. It's the Argent.

21:13.870 --> 21:16.000
Are you all right, Akashi?

21:17.080 --> 21:17.880
He's here!

21:44.570 --> 21:45.700
Akashi-kun?

21:47.240 --> 21:48.950
Sasame...

21:49.660 --> 21:51.410
Welcome back.

21:51.410 --> 21:52.580
Yeah...

21:52.580 --> 21:54.540
You had us worried sick!

21:54.540 --> 21:57.370
Only the pilot suit turned into Necrometal.

21:57.370 --> 21:58.960
His body's completely fine.

21:58.960 --> 21:59.920
That's a relief.

22:02.710 --> 22:06.090
I heard your song, Sasame.

22:07.260 --> 22:11.470
That's why I was able to come back home again.

22:12.390 --> 22:15.980
That's probably the song that I sang.

22:17.440 --> 22:20.020
I see... Thank you.

22:27.740 --> 22:28.950
The sky...

22:29.570 --> 22:31.200
It's just like that day...

22:31.830 --> 22:33.160
So ridiculously blue.

22:44.800 --> 22:55.430
Throwing away all my excuses, I traced over my abrased heart

22:55.430 --> 22:59.980
In the coldness of the locker room,

22:59.980 --> 23:06.440
Was an unfulfilled promise, locked away

23:06.940 --> 23:12.910
Dispel the darkness in this fallen world,

23:12.910 --> 23:17.450
And give me a reason why I should continue living

23:17.450 --> 23:22.830
The meaning of good-byes, the expectations of people,

23:22.830 --> 23:27.710
And the melodies that we played while never crossing paths

23:27.710 --> 23:33.430
I know I must not run away. The only path is straight ahead

23:33.430 --> 23:37.930
Even if this turns out to be a mistake

23:37.930 --> 23:43.520
The whirlpools of destiny will consume all loneliness

23:43.520 --> 23:51.610
It is an unerasable scar, an egoism that cannot be discarded

24:05.040 --> 24:10.050
Episode 11

24:05.040 --> 24:10.050
Red Lament of Cruelty
